2. Data and results produced by this project: CC0 1.0 Universal
===============================================================

Applies to the count matrices and phenotype tables (tag-seq/data/), and to
every result this analysis produces: tag-seq/DESEQ_output/,
tag-seq/gene_tables/, tag-seq/GO_output/, figures/ and
manuscript/supplementary/. The quality-control reports in tag-seq/QC/ are
covered too, subject to the note on them in section 4.

The contributors have dedicated these files to the public domain by waiving all
of their rights to them worldwide under copyright law, including all related
and neighbouring rights, to the extent allowed by law. You can copy, modify,
distribute and use them, even for commercial purposes, without asking
permission. Citing the associated article or this repository (CITATION.cff) is
requested as scholarly practice, not required.

Full legal text: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode


3. The manuscript: not licensed
===============================

manuscript/manuscript.qmd, manuscript/cover-letter.qmd and their rendered
outputs are a draft of an article intended for journal submission. They are
not released under an open licence; the authors retain all rights pending
publication. manuscript/references.bib is bibliographic metadata and may be
reused freely.


4. Third-party material: its own terms
======================================

These files come from elsewhere and are not covered by sections 1-3.

- tag-seq/genome/GCF_006149115.2_Oner_1.1_feature_table.txt and
  tag-seq/sequences/GCF_006149115.2_Oner_1.1_genomic-sequence-lengths.txt:
  derived from NCBI RefSeq assembly GCF_006149115.2. NCBI itself places no
  restrictions on the use or distribution of its data, though the original
  submitters of data may hold rights of their own; see
  https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/home/about/policies/.

- tag-seq/genome/GCF_006149115.2_Oner_1.1_gene_ontology.gaf.gz: Gene Ontology
  annotation generated by NCBI. GO data are made available by the Gene
  Ontology Consortium under CC BY 4.0; see http://geneontology.org/docs/go-citation-policy/.

- tag-seq/genome/kegg_one_gene2pathway.tsv and kegg_one_pathways.tsv:
  responses from the KEGG REST API (tag-seq/genome/kegg_one_SOURCE.txt).
  KEGG is not a public database: the API is provided for academic use by
  academic users, and non-academic use requires a licence; see
  https://www.kegg.jp/kegg/legal.html. These files are not released under
  any licence in this repository.

- manuscript/apa.csl: the APA 7th edition style from the Citation Style
  Language project, licensed CC BY-SA 3.0
  (http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/).

- manuscript/reference-manuscript.docx: derived from pandoc's default
  reference document, and subject to pandoc's licensing.

- renv/activate.R: generated by renv (MIT, Posit Software, PBC).

- archive/david-2023/: output of the DAVID web service, subject to DAVID's
  terms of use.

- tag-seq/QC/multiqc_gonad/*.html: reports generated by MultiQC (GPL-3.0),
  which embed JavaScript libraries under their own licences. The data in them
  are covered by section 2.
